ing\",\"headline\":\"Genshin Lunar Reactions Guide — Moonsign, Triggers, Scaling\",\"description\":\"How Genshin's Lunar and Stellar Glimmer reactions work: which characters enable them, Moonsign levels, CRIT rules and the 60/30/5/5 team damage split.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-08-17T00:00:00.000Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-09-04T00:00:00.000Z\",\"author\":{\"@id\":\"https://gamertagmythras.com/#person-mythras\"},\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://gamertagmythras.com/#organization\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://gamertagmythras.com/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide\"},\"keywords\":\"genshin lunar reactions, lunar-charged genshin, lunar-bloom explained, moonsign ascendant gleam, stellar-conduct genshin, stellar swirl reaction, can lunar reactions crit\",\"articleSection\":\"Advanced Strategy\",\"wordCount\":2581,\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":true,\"speakable\":{\"@type\":\"SpeakableSpecification\",\"cssSelector\":[\"#blog-tldr\",\"h1\"]},\"image\":\"https://gamertagmythras.com/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/hero-columbina.webp\"}3e:Td62,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What are the Lunar reactions in Genshin Impact?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The Lunar reactions are Lunar-Charged (Electro + Hydro), Lunar-Bloom (Dendro + Hydro) and Lunar-Crystallize (Geo + Hydro). They are converted versions of Electro-Charged, Bloom and Hydro Crystallize, and they only occur when a character with the matching Moonsign Benediction passive — Ineffa, Flins, Lauma, Nefer, Zibai, Linnea or Columbina — is in the party. Unlike their base reactions, Lunar reactions can deal CRIT hits.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can Lunar reactions CRIT in Genshin?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. Lunar and Stellar Glimmer reaction damage uses the contributing characters' ordinary CRIT Rate and CRIT DMG, unlike classic transformative reactions such as Electro-Charged or Superconduct, which cannot CRIT by default. For the combined indirect damage instance, whether the hit counts as a CRIT is determined by whether the highest-ranked contributor's individual result was a CRIT.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is Moonsign and what does Ascendant Gleam do?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Moonsign is a Genshin team bonus that scales with the number of Moonsign characters in the party: one gives Nascent Gleam, two gives Ascendant Gleam. At Ascendant Gleam, Moonsign characters have certain talents and skills enhanced, and for 20 seconds after a non-Moonsign character uses a skill or burst they boost all nearby characters' Lunar Reaction damage by up to 36 percent, scaling off their own ATK, Max HP, DEF or Elemental Mastery depending on their element.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which characters enable Lunar-Charged?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Three characters convert Electro-Charged into Lunar-Charged: Ineffa (Assemblage Hub passive), Flins (Old World Secrets) and Columbina (Moonlight, Lent Unto You). Ineffa and Flins each add up to 14 percent to Lunar-Charged's base damage from their own ATK, while Columbina adds up to 7 percent from her Max HP and is the only character who also converts Bloom and Hydro Crystallize into their Lunar versions at the same time.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How does Elemental Mastery scale Lunar reaction damage?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Lunar and Stellar Glimmer reactions use the formula 6 x EM / (EM + 2000) for their Elemental Mastery bonus — roughly 54.5 percent at 200 EM and 200 percent at 1,000 EM. That is a much flatter curve than the 16-coefficient formula classic transformative reactions use, which pays 533 percent at the same 1,000 EM. Because Lunar reactions can also CRIT, contributors want a balanced build with level 90, CRIT stats and EM rather than pure EM stacking.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is Stellar Swirl in Genshin?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Stellar Swirl is a Stellar Glimmer reaction added in Genshin Impact Version 7.0 on 12 August 2026. When Sandrone, Odette or the Cryo Traveler is in the party, a Cryo Swirl — Anemo hitting a Cryo or Cryo-Freeze aura — becomes Stellar Swirl instead. Like ordinary Swirl, its indirect damage applies its element and can chain into further reactions, and Stellar Glimmer reactions also disable certain attacks used by the Snowland Fae and Aberrant Chimeric Monsters enemy groups.\"}}]}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1f:[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$3d\"}}],[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Home\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://gamertagmythras.com/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":2,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Blog\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://gamertagmythras.com/blog\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":3,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Genshin Impact\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://gamertagmythras.com/blog/genshin-impact\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":4,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Genshin Lunar Reactions Guide — Moonsign, Triggers, Scaling\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://gamertagmythras.com/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide\\\"}]}\"}}],[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$3e\"}}],\"$undefined\",null,\"$L3f\",\"$L40\",\"$L41\",\"$L42\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,":HL[\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/hero-columbina.webp\",\"image\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3f:[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-28 md:pt-32 pb-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-xs text-[#9999aa] mb-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog\",\"className\":\"hover:text-[#F0C850] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Blog\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#55556a]\",\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact\",\"className\":\"hover:text-[#F0C850] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Genshin\"}],[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#55556a]\",\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-1 rounded-md bg-[#D4A853]/10 text-[#F0C850] font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-[10px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"🧠\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Advanced Strategy\"}]]}]]]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white leading-tight tracking-tight mb-5\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.01em\"},\"children\":\"Genshin Lunar Reactions Guide — Moonsign, Triggers, Scaling\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-6\",\"children\":\"Genshin has quietly added five reactions since Version 5.8, and they break the oldest rules in the combat system: they CRIT, they ignore DMG Bonus and enemy DEF, and they refuse to fire at all unless the right character is standing in your party.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs text-[#9999aa] pb-6 border-b border-[#D4A853]/15\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Published \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white font-medium\",\"children\":\"August 17, 2026\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Updated \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white font-medium\",\"children\":\"September 4, 2026\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#55556a]\",\"children\":\"·\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[13,\" min read\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#55556a]\",\"children\":\"·\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"By \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/about\",\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] hover:text-[#F0C850] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Mythras\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"40:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 mb-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/hero-columbina.webp\",\"alt\":\"Columbina, the only character whose Moonsign Benediction passive converts Electro-Charged, Bloom and Hydro Crystallize into all three Lunar reactions at once.\",\"className\":\"w-full rounded-xl border border-[#D4A853]/15\",\"width\":1200,\"height\":630}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"41:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"aside\",null,{\"id\":\"blog-tldr\",\"className\":\"my-8 rounded-xl border border-[#D4A853]/30 bg-[#D4A853]/[0.06] p-5 md:p-6\",\"aria-label\":\"TL;DR — quick answer\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2 mb-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase\",\"children\":\"TL;DR\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-[#D4A853]/40 to-transparent\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#f0f0f5] text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed font-medium\",\"children\":\"Genshin's Lunar reactions (Lunar-Charged, Lunar-Bloom, Lunar-Crystallize) and Stellar Glimmer reactions (Stellar-Conduct, Stellar Swirl) only fire when an enabler character converts the base reaction — Ineffa, Flins, Lauma, Nefer, Zibai, Linnea or Columbina for Lunar, and Sandrone, Odette or the Cryo Traveler for Stellar. Unlike classic transformative reactions they can CRIT, their EM bonus follows 6 x EM / (EM + 2000), and they ignore DMG Bonus and enemy DEF; indirect Lunar-Charged, Lunar-Crystallize and Stellar Swirl damage also combines up to four contributors' stats weighted 60/30/5/5. Two Moonsign characters put the party at Ascendant Gleam, which adds up to 36 percent more Lunar damage from non-Moonsign teammates.\"}]]}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-[#D4A853]/15 bg-[#0c0c18]/60 p-5 my-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-[#D4A853]/70 mb-3\",\"children\":\"Table of Contents\"}],[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#the-reaction-chart-grew-while-you-were-farming\",\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] hover:text-[#F0C850] transition-colors flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853]/60 text-xs mt-0.5\",\"children\":\"·\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"The Reaction Chart Grew While You Were Farming\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#five-new-reactions-and-the-characters-that-switch-them-on\",\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] hover:text-[#F0C850] transition-colors flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853]/60 text-xs mt-0.5\",\"children\":\"·\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Five New Reactions, and the Characters That Switch Them On\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#the-rules-that-changed-crit-contributors-and-the-60-30-5-5-split\",\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] hover:text-[#F0C85