text-[#9999aa] leading-relaxed line-clamp-3\",\"children\":\"Xingqiu drops exactly five Hydro particles per skill cast. Standing on him when they land is worth 15 Energy. Swapping away first is worth 9. Same cooldown, same rotation, six Energy gone — and that is before you touch the Energy Recharge stat at all.\"}]\n5b:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-semibold text-[#D4A853] group-hover:gap-2 transition-all\",\"children\":[\"Read article\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"→\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5c:[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"genshin-elemental-reactions-guide\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-elemental-reactions-guide\",\"className\":\"group block glass-panel rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-[#D4A853]/10 hover:border-[#D4A853]/40 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"aspect-video bg-[#0c0c18] overflow-hidden border-b border-[#D4A853]/10\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-elemental-reactions-guide/hero-nahida.webp\",\"alt\":\"Nahida, the Dendro Archon, whose kit made Dendro reactions like Hyperbloom and Aggravate the backbone of modern Genshin Impact team building.\",\"loading\":\"lazy\",\"className\":\"w-full h-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.03] transition-transform duration-300\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"p-5 md:p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 mb-3 text-xs text-[#9999aa]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-1 rounded-md bg-[#D4A853]/10 text-[#F0C850] font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-[10px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"🧠\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Advanced Strategy\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Jul 20, 2026\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#55556a]\",\"children\":\"·\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[12,\" min read\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#F0C850] transition-colors leading-snug mb-2\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.01em\"},\"children\":\"Genshin Elemental Reactions Guide — Every Multiplier Explained\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-[#9999aa] leading-relaxed line-clamp-3\",\"children\":\"Most players know Hydro plus Pyro equals Vaporize. Far fewer know that swapping which element lands first is the difference between a 2x multiplier and a 1.5x one — the same rotation, a third of the damage gone.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-semibold text-[#D4A853] group-hover:gap-2 transition-all\",\"children\":[\"Read article\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"→\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5d:[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"genshin-flins-build-guide\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-flins-build-guide\",\"className\":\"group block glass-panel rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-[#D4A853]/10 hover:border-[#D4A853]/40 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"aspect-video bg-[#0c0c18] overflow-hidden border-b border-[#D4A853]/10\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-flins-build-guide/hero-flins.webp\",\"alt\":\"Flins, Genshin Impact's Nod-Krai Lightkeeper, in his character showcase art with his lantern-spear Pocztowy Demonspear.\",\"loading\":\"lazy\",\"className\":\"w-full h-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.03] transition-transform duration-300\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"p-5 md:p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 mb-3 text-xs text-[#9999aa]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-1 rounded-md bg-[#D4A853]/10 text-[#F0C850] font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-[10px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"⚔️\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Team Builds\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Sep 4, 2026\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#55556a]\",\"children\":\"·\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[12,\" min read\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#F0C850] transition-colors leading-snug mb-2\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.01em\"},\"children\":\"Genshin Flins Build Guide — Talents, Weapon, Artifacts\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-[#9999aa] leading-relaxed line-clamp-3\",\"children\":\"Flins does not poke a shield and walk away. His whole kit is a two-stage transformation that turns his own Elemental Skill and Burst into direct Lunar-Charged hits, which means the stat priorities and artifact math for a normal Electro DPS do not apply to him. Here is what actually moves his damage, talent by talent.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-semibold text-[#D4A853] group-hover:gap-2 transition-all\",\"children\":[\"Read article\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"→\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5e:[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"genshin-artifact-guide\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-artifact-guide\",\"className\":\"group block glass-panel rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-[#D4A853]/10 hover:border-[#D4A853]/40 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"aspect-video bg-[#0c0c18] overflow-hidden border-b border-[#D4A853]/10\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-artifact-guide/hero-hu-tao.webp\",\"alt\":\"Hu Tao, a Pyro carry whose damage output depends almost entirely on artifact substat quality rather than character investment.\",\"loading\":\"lazy\",\"className\":\"w-full h-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.03] transition-transform duration-300\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"p-5 md:p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 mb-3 text-xs text-[#9999aa]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-1 rounded-md bg-[#D4A853]/10 text-[#F0C850] font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-[10px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"🎮\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Game Guides\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Jul 20, 2026\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#55556a]\",\"children\":\"·\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[13,\" min read\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#F0C850] transition-colors leading-snug mb-2\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.01em\"},\"children\":\"Genshin Artifact Guide — Stats, Rolls and Resin Math\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-[#9999aa] leading-relaxed line-clamp-3\",\"children\":\"A five-star artifact can roll the exact same substat four times and give you anywhere from 10.88 percent to 15.54 percent CRIT DMG. Understanding that spread is the difference between a functional account and a museum of half-built characters.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-semibold text-[#D4A853] group-hover:gap-2 transition-all\",\"children\":[\"Read article\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"→\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5f:[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"genshin-stygian-onslaught-guide\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-stygian-onslaught-guide\",\"className\":\"group block glass-panel rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-[#D4A853]/10 hover:border-[#D4A853]/40 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"aspect-video bg-[#0c0c18] overflow-hidden border-b border-[#D4A853]/10\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-stygian-onslaught-guide/hero-stygian-onslaught.webp\",\"alt\":\"The unlocked Stygian Onslaught event menu in Genshin Impact, showing the ley line disturbance challenge at Sal Terrae in Liyue.\",\"loading\":\"lazy\",\"className\":\"w-full h-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.03] transition-transform duration-300\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"p-5 md:p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 mb-3 text-xs text-[#9999aa]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-1 rounded-md bg-[#D4A853]/10 text-[#F0C850] font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-[10px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"🧠\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Advanced Strategy\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Aug 15, 2026\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#55556a]\",\"children\":\"·\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[14,\" min read\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#F0C850] transition-colors leading-snug mb-2\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.01em\"},\"children\":\"Genshin Stygian Onslaught Guide — The Primogems Stop at Difficulty Three\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-[#9999aa] leading-relaxed line-clamp-3\",\"children\":\"Genshin has three permanent endgames. The third one hands you its entire Primogem payout at difficulty three of six, then spends the top half of the ladder paying you in artifact currency and weapon skins instead. The reward table is the whole strategy.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-semibold text-[#D4A853] group-hover:gap-2 transition-all\",\"children\":[\"Read article\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"→\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,":HL[\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/lunar-charged-thundercloud.webp\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/moonsign-icon.webp\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/lauma-lunar-bloom.webp\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/stellar-swirl-announcement.webp\",\"image\"]\n60:[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Electro-Charged\"}]\n61:[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-3\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Ineffa, Flins, Columbina\"}]\n62:[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-4\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Version 5.8\"}]\n63:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-1\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Lunar-Bloom\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Dendro + Hydro\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Bloom\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-3\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Lauma, Nefer, Columbina\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-4\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Version Luna I\"}]]}]\n64:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-2\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Lunar-Crystallize\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Geo + Hydro\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Hydro Crystallize\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-3\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Zibai, Linnea, Columbina\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-4\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Version Luna IV\"}]]}]\n65:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-3\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Stellar-Conduct\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Cryo + Electro\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Superconduct\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-3\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Sandrone, Odette, Cryo Traveler\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-4\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Version Luna VIII\"}]]}]\n66:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-4\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Stellar Swirl\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Anemo + Cryo\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Cryo Swirl\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-3\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Sandrone, Odette, Cryo Traveler\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-4\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Version 7.0\"}]]}]\n67:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Two things to read off that table. First, Columbina is the outlier on the Lunar side — her Moonlight, Lent Unto You passive converts all three base reactions at once, where every other Lunar enabler converts exactly one. Second, the Stellar side is more economical: all three Stellar enablers convert both Superconduct and Cryo Swirl, so one of Sandrone, Odette or the Cryo Traveler unlocks the whole Stellar family.\"}]\n68:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"The conversion is total, not optional. With Ineffa in the party, your Electro-Charged \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"em-0\",{\"className\":\"italic text-[#F0D68A]\",\"children\":\"is\"}],\" Lunar-Charged — there is no toggle. Each enabler also carries a personal Base DMG bonus for the reaction they enable, scaling off their own signature stat: Ineffa and Flins add up to 14 percent from ATK, Lauma and Nefer up to 14 percent from Elemental Mastery, Zibai and Linnea up to 14 percent from DEF, and Columbina up to 7 percent from Max HP.\"]}]\n69:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",\"img-0\",{\"src\":\""])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/lunar-charged-thundercloud.webp\",\"alt\":\"The Lunar-Charged thundercloud dealing Electro damage over a fight, from Ineffa's official character details.\",\"className\":\"rounded-lg my-6 max-w-full border border-[#D4A853]/15\"}]}]\n6a:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"id\":\"the-rules-that-changed-crit-contributors-and-the-60-30-5-5-split\",\"className\":\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-[#D4A853]/15 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\"},\"children\":\"The Rules That Changed — CRIT, Contributors and the 60-30-5-5 Split\"}]\n6b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Classic transformative reactions — Electro-Charged, Superconduct, Bloom and the rest — cannot CRIT by default, scale off one character's level and Elemental Mastery, and ignore everything else. Their Lunar and Stellar replacements tear that up in three ways.\"}]\n6c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"They CRIT.\"}],\" Lunar and Stellar Glimmer damage uses the contributors' ordinary CRIT Rate and CRIT DMG — the same stats your on-hit damage uses, not a special reaction stat. Whether the combined hit counts as a CRIT (for things like the Favonius weapon passives) is decided by whether the top contributor's roll was a CRIT.\"]}]\n6d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Everyone contributes.\"}],\" For indirect Lunar-Charged, Lunar-Crystallize and Stellar Swirl damage, the game runs a full damage calculation for every character who applied one of the reaction's elements — their level, Elemental Mastery, reaction bonuses and CRIT — then combines the results by rank: the highest individual result counts at 60 percent, the second at 30 percent, and the third and fourth at 5 percent each. Fewer contributors simply drop entries without inflating the rest, which means a lone contributor's reaction lands at 60 percent weight and a second contributor is worth their entire result at 30 percent on top. The old rule — aura character's stats never matter — is dead here. In a Lunar team, your applier's build is part of the reaction's damage.\"]}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"The scaling knobs moved.\"}],\" The Elemental Mastery bonus for Lunar and Stellar reactions follows 6 × EM / (EM + 2000) — a much flatter curve than the 16-coefficient formula classic transformative reactions use. At 200 EM that is a 54.5 percent bonus; at 1,000 EM it is 200 percent, where a transformative reaction at the same 1,000 EM gets 533 percent. Meanwhile the level multiplier still applies (1,446.85 for a level 90 character), and the damage ignores DMG Bonus goblets and enemy DEF but is still cut by elemental RES. The practical read: EM is still good, but it is no longer the only stat — CRIT and the contributor mechanic mean Lunar teams reward real, rounded builds.\"]}]\n6f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Base reaction coefficients, for the people who run the numbers:\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"70:[\"$\",\"div\",\"table-1\",{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto mb-6 rounded-lg border border-[#D4A853]/15\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"table\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full text-sm text-left\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"thead\",\"thead-0\",{\"className\":\"bg-[#D4A853]/10 text-[#F0C850] uppercase text-xs tracking-wider\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-0\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"th\",\"th-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Reaction\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",\"th-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Indirect coefficient\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",\"th-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Direct coefficient\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"tbody\",\"tbody-0\",{\"className\":\"divide-y divide-[#D4A853]/10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-0\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Lunar-Charged\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"3\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"3\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-1\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Lunar-Bloom\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"— (no indirect DMG)\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"1\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-2\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Lunar-Crystallize\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"1.6\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"1.6\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-3\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Stellar-Conduct\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"— (no indirect DMG)\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"1 to 2, scaling with Polestar Field hits\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-4\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Stellar Swirl\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"0.75 initial, 2 at Lv. 1, 3 at Lv. 2\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"1\"}]]}]]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"71:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"id\":\"moonsign-is-the-team-bonus-lunar-damage-scales-on\",\"className\":\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-[#D4A853]/15 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\"},\"children\":\"Moonsign Is the Team Bonus Lunar Damage Scales On\"}]\n72:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Every Lunar enabler raises the party's Moonsign by one level, and the level is a team-wide bonus in its own right — it sits alongside Elemental Resonance on the party screen.\"}]\n73:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-13\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"One Moonsign character puts the party at \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Nascent Gleam\"}],\". Two puts it at \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-1\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Ascendant Gleam\"}],\", which does two things: it enhances certain talents and skills of the Moonsign characters themselves, and it turns your non-Moonsign teammates into Lunar damage batteries. For 20 seconds after a non-Moonsign character casts a skill or burst, they boost the Lunar Reaction damage of all nearby characters based on their own element's signature stat, capped at 36 percent:\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"74:[\"$\",\"div\",\"table-2\",{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto mb-6 rounded-lg border border-[#D4A853]/15\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"table\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full text-sm text-left\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"thead\",\"thead-0\",{\"className\":\"bg-[#D4A853]/10 text-[#F0C850] uppercase text-xs tracking-wider\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-0\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"th\",\"th-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Non-Moonsign character's element\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",\"th-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Rate\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",\"th-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Stat needed for the 36% cap\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"tbody\",\"tbody-0\",{\"className\":\"divide-y divide-[#D4A853]/10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-0\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Pyro, Electro or Cryo\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"0.9% per 100 ATK\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"4,000 ATK\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-1\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Hydro\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"0.6% per 1,000 Max HP\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"60,000 Max HP\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-2\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Geo\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"1% per 100 DEF\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"3,600 DEF\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tr-3\",{\"className\":\"hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-0\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"Anemo or Dendro\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-1\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"2.25% per 100 Elemental Mastery\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",\"td-2\",{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-[#c8c8d4]\",\"children\":\"1,600 Elemental Mastery\"}]]}]]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"75:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-14\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"That table quietly redefines what a \\\"support stat\\\" is in a Lunar team. A Hydro character sitting on a huge HP pool, or an Anemo unit stacked with EM, is contributing Lunar damage just by existing and pressing their skill on cooldown. When you are picking the third and fourth slots of a Lunar-Charged team, this table is the tiebreaker.\"}]\n76:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-15\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",\"img-0\",{\"src\":\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/moonsign-icon.webp\",\"alt\":\"The Moonsign team bonus icon from the party setup screen.\",\"className\":\"rounded-lg my-6 max-w-full border border-[#D4A853]/15\"}]}]\n77:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-4\",{\"id\":\"what-each-reaction-actually-does\",\"className\":\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-[#D4A853]/15 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\"},\"children\":\"What Each Reaction Actually Does\"}]\n78:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"h3-0\",{\"id\":\"lunar-charged-parks-a-thundercloud-over-the-fight\",\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#F0C850] mt-8 mb-3 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.02em\"},\"children\":\"Lunar-Charged Parks a Thundercloud Over the Fight\"}]\n79:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-16\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Lunar-Charged spawns a thundercloud that positions itself between your party and its targets and deals Electro damage every 2 seconds to opponents affected by both Wet and Electro. Each damage tick consumes 0.4 gauge units of both auras at once. The cloud lasts 6 seconds, refreshes its duration on a new Lunar-Charged trigger, and only one can exist at a time — trigger the reaction outside the cloud's range and a new cloud replaces the old one at the new location.\"}]\n7a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-17\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"With a coefficient of 3, plus CRIT scaling and the contributor split, this is the workhorse of the Lunar family. Ineffa and \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-flins-build-guide\",\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] underline decoration-[#D4A853]/30 underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#F0C850] hover:decoration-[#D4A853]/70 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Flins\"}],\" are its dedicated enablers.\"]}]\n7b:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"h3-1\",{\"id\":\"lunar-bloom-deals-nothing-on-its-own\",\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#F0C850] mt-8 mb-3 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.02em\"},\"children\":\"Lunar-Bloom Deals Nothing on Its Own\"}]\n7c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-18\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Lunar-Bloom is the odd one out: it deals no damage when triggered. On the current patch, Lunar-Bloom damage comes only from character talents and constellations — Lauma and Nefer are built to convert Bloom and then pump the resulting Lunar-Bloom numbers themselves. The Dendro Cores it creates are identical to ordinary Bloom cores, and the cores' own damage does not count as Lunar-Bloom damage.\"}]\n7d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-19\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"Triggering it also banks \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Verdant Dew\"}],\", a stackable resource capped at 3 that persists through party changes, teleports, daily resets and even logging out. If you run Lauma or Nefer, the reaction is their engine rather than a standalone payoff.\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-20\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",\"img-0\",{\"src\":\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/lauma-lunar-bloom.webp\",\"alt\":\"Lauma, whose Nature's Chorus passive converts every Bloom reaction the party triggers into Lunar-Bloom.\",\"className\":\"rounded-lg my-6 max-w-full border border-[#D4A853]/15\"}]}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"h3"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"-2\",{\"id\":\"lunar-crystallize-counts-to-three\",\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#F0C850] mt-8 mb-3 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.02em\"},\"children\":\"Lunar-Crystallize Counts to Three\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-21\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"When Geo hits a Hydro aura with Zibai, Linnea or Columbina in the party, Crystallize becomes Lunar-Crystallize and creates three \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Moondrifts\"}],\" around the target. While Moondrifts are on the field, every third Lunar-Crystallize reaction makes them resonate — Moondrift Harmony — firing a homing projectile that deals Geo damage at a 1.6 coefficient.\"]}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-22\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Moondrifts count as Geo constructs, and the Geo resonance (Enduring Rock) has been rewritten around them: characters near a Moondrift get the same 15 percent damage boost and 20 percent Geo RES shred that shielded characters get.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"h3-3\",{\"id\":\"stellar-conduct-builds-a-field-that-pays-by-the-hit\",\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#F0C850] mt-8 mb-3 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.02em\"},\"children\":\"Stellar-Conduct Builds a Field That Pays by the Hit\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-23\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Stellar-Conduct converts Superconduct when Sandrone, Odette or the Cryo Traveler is in the party, and like Lunar-Bloom it deals no damage on its own — its damage comes from those characters' talents, landing as either Cryo or Electro depending on the source.\"}]\n84:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-24\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"What it does do is create a \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Starlight Prism\"}],\" that sustains a Polestar Field for 7 seconds. The Prism counts Cryo and Electro hits that apply their element inside the field, resetting every 4 seconds, and pays out on the count: the reaction's base coefficient jumps from 1 to 1.45 at one recorded hit and climbs by 0.05 per hit to 2 at twelve; the field's Cryo and Electro DMG Bonus starts at 20 percent and climbs to 40; and every enemy inside loses 40 percent Physical RES — the same shred Superconduct gave. It is a reaction that pays you for attacking fast, which is exactly what Cryo-Electro teams already do.\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"h3-4\",{\"id\":\"stellar-swirl-is-the-one-that-chains\",\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-[#F0C850] mt-8 mb-3 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.02em\"},\"children\":\"Stellar Swirl Is the One That Chains\"}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-25\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Stellar Swirl arrived with Version 7.0 and converts Cryo Swirl — Anemo hitting a Cryo aura, including a Cryo-created Freeze aura. It is the only new reaction that keeps Swirl's signature trick: indirect Stellar Swirl applies its element onward, so it can trigger further reactions down the line, using the initial trigger's stats. Its indirect coefficient starts at 0.75 for the initial reaction and rises to 2 and 3 at its Lv. 1 and Lv. 2 states.\"}]\n87:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-26\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"It also has teeth in the new region: Stellar Glimmer reactions disable certain attacks of the Snowland Fae and Aberrant Chimeric Monsters, the enemy groups Version 7.0 shipped. Stygian Onslaught has already started keying boss shields to these reactions — the Savage Tremors iteration's Whisperer of Nightmares took bonus shield damage from Lunar Reaction DMG, covered in our \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-stygian-onslaught-guide\",\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] underline decoration-[#D4A853]/30 underline-"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"offset-2 hover:text-[#F0C850] hover:decoration-[#D4A853]/70 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Stygian Onslaught guide\"}],\".\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-27\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",\"img-0\",{\"src\":\"/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/stellar-swirl-announcement.webp\",\"alt\":\"HoYoverse's official announcement panel for Stellar Swirl, the Stellar Glimmer reaction added in Version 7.0.\",\"className\":\"rounded-lg my-6 max-w-full border border-[#D4A853]/15\"}]}]\n89:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-5\",{\"id\":\"building-for-lunar-and-stellar-damage\",\"className\":\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-[#D4A853]/15 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\"},\"children\":\"Building for Lunar and Stellar Damage\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-28\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"The artifact system has caught up with the mechanics, and the new sets are where builds should start.\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-29\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"Three sets serve Lunar teams. \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Night of the Sky's Unveiling\"}],\" gives 80 EM on two pieces, and its four-piece grants Gleaming Moon: Intent — 15 or 30 percent CRIT Rate depending on whether the party sits at Nascent or Ascendant Gleam. \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-1\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Silken Moon's Serenade\"}],\" runs 20 percent Energy Recharge on two pieces and feeds the whole party 60 or 120 EM from off-field. \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-2\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Aubade of Morningstar and Moon\"}],\" gives 80 EM and boosts Lunar Reaction damage by 20 percent while its wearer is off field, rising by a further 40 percent at Ascendant Gleam. Each distinct Gleaming Moon effect in the party also adds 10 percent Lunar Reaction damage for everyone, which nudges Lunar teams toward spreading the sets across members rather than stacking one. Stellar teams get \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-3\",{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Heart of the Furnace\"}],\": 18 percent ATK on two pieces, and a four-piece that adds 12 percent ATK to the wearer and 50 percent Stellar Glimmer reaction damage to the party when they trigger one.\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-30\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"Resonance picked up Lunar clauses too. High Voltage (double Electro) now guarantees its Electro particle on Lunar-Charged and Stellar-Conduct triggers, and Sprawling Greenery (double Dendro) hands out its 30 EM party buff on Lunar-Bloom.\"}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-31\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"As for stats: the flat 6-coefficient EM curve means you stop short of the 1,000-EM piles that \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-elemental-reactions-guide\",\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] underline decoration-[#D4A853]/30 underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#F0C850] hover:decoration-[#D4A853]/70 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Hyperbloom triggers\"}],\" wear. Contributors want level 90 first — the level multiplier is the biggest single number in the formula — then a working CRIT build, then EM. And because up to four characters contribute at 60/30/5/5, a Lunar team has no true stat-stick passenger; the \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"a-1\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-damage-formula-guide\",\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] underline decoration-[#D4A853]/30 underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#F0C850] hover:decoration-[#D4A853]/70 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"damage formula\"}],\" is now being run on everybody.\"]}]\n8e:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-6\",{\"id\":\"what-still-holds-from-the-classic-reaction-rules\",\"className\":\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-[#D4A853]/15 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\"},\"children\":\"What Still Holds From the Classic Reaction Rules\"}]\n8f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-32\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"The classic chart is untouched underneath. Vaporize is still 2x for Hydro-onto-Pyro, Melt still flips it, aura decay and internal cooldown still decide whether anything fires at all, and in a party with no enabler the five new reactions simply do not exist — Electro plus Hydro is the same Electro-Charged it was in 2020. Our \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-elemental-reactions-guide\",\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] underline decoration-[#D4A853]/30 underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#F0C850] hover:decoration-[#D4A853]/70 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"elemental reactions guide\"}],\" covers that foundation; note that it predates the Lunar era, so its \\\"four families\\\" framing and its trigger-stats-only rule describe the classic set, not these five.\"]}]\n90:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-33\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":\"The mental shift worth making is this: classic reactions are something any team does by accident. Lunar and Stellar reactions are something you build a roster for on purpose — one enabler minimum, two Moonsign characters for Ascendant Gleam, and third and fourth slots chosen off the 36-percent buff table. That is a different team-building question than classic reactions ask.\"}]\n91:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-34\",{\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[15px] md:text-base\",\"children\":[\"More Genshin coverage lives on the \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/blog/genshin-impact\",\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] underline decoration-[#D4A853]/30 underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#F0C850] hover:decoration-[#D4A853]/70 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Genshin Impact coverage hub\"}],\", and the rest of our game guides are on the \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",\"a-1\",{\"href\":\"/blog\",\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] underline decoration-[#D4A853]/30 underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#F0C850] hover:decoration-[#D4A853]/70 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Mythras blog\"}],\".\"]}]\n92:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-7\",{\"id\":\"quick-action-checklist\",\"className\":\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-[#D4A853]/15 scroll-mt-24\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-display)\"},\"children\":\"Quick Action Checklist\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"93:[\"$\",\"ul\",\"ul-0\",{\"className\":\"list-disc list-outside pl-6 mb-5 space-y-2 text-[#c8c8d4] marker:text-[#D4A853]/60\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Lunar and Stellar reactions only exist while an enabler is in the party: Ineffa/Flins (Lunar-Charged), Lauma/Nefer (Lunar-Bloom), Zibai/Linnea (Lunar-Crystallize), Columbina (all three), Sandrone/Odette/Cryo Traveler (both Stellar reactions).\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"They can CRIT with ordinary CRIT stats, ignore DMG Bonus and enemy DEF, and are reduced by elemental RES.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Indirect Lunar-Charged, Lunar-Crystallize and Stellar Swirl damage combines every contributor's individually calculated result at 60/30/5/5 by rank — appliers' builds now matter.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-3\",{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The EM bonus is 6 × EM / (EM + 2000): 54.5 percent at 200 EM, 200 percent at 1,000 EM. Flatter than classic transformative scaling, so build CRIT alongside EM.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-4\",{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"One Moonsign character = Nascent Gleam; two = Ascendant Gleam, which buffs Moonsign characters and lets non-Moonsign teammates add up to 36 percent Lunar damage off ATK, HP, DEF or EM.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-5\",{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Lunar-Bloom and Stellar-Conduct deal no damage on their own — their numbers come from enabler talents, so do not run them without Lauma, Nefer or a Stellar enabler built for it.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-6\",{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Lunar-Crystallize fires a homing Geo projectile every third trigger while Moondrifts stand; Moondrifts are Geo constructs and feed the reworked Enduring Rock resonance.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-7\",{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Stellar-Conduct keeps Superconduct's 40 percent Physical RES shred inside its Polestar Field, and its coefficient climbs from 1.45 to 2 as the field records up to 12 Cryo/Electro hits.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-8\",{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Artifact sets: Night of the Sky's Unveiling, Silken Moon's Serenade and Aubade of Morningstar and Moon for Lunar; Heart of the Furnace for Stellar.\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"94:[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"blog-faq\",\"open\":false,\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-[#D4A853]/15 bg-[#0c0c18]/60 overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"cursor-pointer list-none [\u0026::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left p-4 md:p-5 hover:bg-[#D4A853]/[0.03] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-white pr-4\",\"children\":\"Which characters enable Lunar-Charged?\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45\",\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"+\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 md:px-5 pb-5 text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Three characters convert Electro-Charged into Lunar-Charged: Ineffa (Assemblage Hub passive), Flins (Old World Secrets) and Columbina (Moonlight, Lent Unto You). Ineffa and Flins each add up to 14 percent to Lunar-Charged's base damage from their own ATK, while Columbina adds up to 7 percent from her Max HP and is the only character who also converts Bloom and Hydro Crystallize into their Lunar versions at the same time.\"}]]}]\n95:[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"blog-faq\",\"open\":false,\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-[#D4A853]/15 bg-[#0c0c18]/60 overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"cursor-pointer list-none [\u0026::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left p-4 md:p-5 hover:bg-[#D4A853]/[0.03] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-white pr-4\",\"children\":\"How does Elemental Mastery scale Lunar reaction damage?\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45\",\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"+\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 md:px-5 pb-5 text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Lunar and Stellar Glimmer reactions use the formula 6 x EM / (EM + 2000) for their Elemental Mastery bonus — roughly 54.5 percent at 200 EM and 200 percent at 1,000 EM. That is a much flatter curve than the 16-coefficient formula classic transformative reactions use, which pays 533 percent at the same 1,000 EM. Because Lunar reactions can also CRIT, contributors want a balanced build with level 90, CRIT stats and EM rather than pure EM stacking.\"}]]}]\n96:[\"$\",\"details\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"blog-faq\",\"open\":false,\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-[#D4A853]/15 bg-[#0c0c18]/60 overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"cursor-pointer list-none [\u0026::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left p-4 md:p-5 hover:bg-[#D4A853]/[0.03] transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-white pr-4\",\"children\":\"What is Stellar Swirl in Genshin?\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45\",\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"+\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 md:px-5 pb-5 text-[#c8c8d4] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Stellar Swirl is a Stellar Glimmer reaction added in Genshin Impact Version 7.0 on 12 August 2026. When Sandrone, Odette or the Cryo Traveler is in the party, a Cryo Swirl — Anemo hitting a Cryo or Cryo-Freeze aura — becomes Stellar Swirl instead. Like ordinary Swirl, its indirect damage applies its element and can chain into further reactions, and Stellar Glimmer reactions also disable certain attacks used by the Snowland Fae and Aberrant Chimeric Monsters enemy groups.\"}]]}]\n99:[\"$\",\"li\",\"11\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.hoyolab.com/article/46135087\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-[#c8c8d4] hover:text-[#F0C850] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"HoYoverse (HoYoLAB) — official announcement of the Stellar Swirl reaction for Version 7.0\"}]}]\n9a:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 flex items-center justify-between\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[11px] text-[#9999aa]\",\"children\":\"on Amazon\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"c"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"lassName\":\"text-[#D4A853] text-sm font-semibold group-hover:translate-x-0.5 transition-transform\",\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"View ↗\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"9b:[\"$\",\"a\",\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=usb%20c%20power%20bank\u0026tag=mythras2026-20-2\",{\"href\":\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=usb%20c%20power%20bank\u0026tag=mythras2026-20\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer sponsored\",\"data-mythras-asin\":\"$undefined\",\"data-mythras-kind\":\"search\",\"data-mythras-placement\":\"post-grid\",\"data-mythras-game\":\"genshin-impact\",\"className\":\"group flex flex-col rounded-lg border border-[#D4A853]/15 bg-[#12121f]/60 overflow-hidden hover:border-[#D4A853]/40 transition-all\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative aspect-[4/3] bg-[#0c0c18] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-shopping-bag w-8 h-8 text-[#D4A853]/25\",\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1ltviw\",{\"d\":\"M16 10a4 4 0 0 1-8 0\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"awc11p\",{\"d\":\"M3.103 6.034h17.794\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"o988cm\",{\"d\":\"M3.4 5.467a2 2 0 0 0-.4 1.2V20a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V6.667a2 2 0 0 0-.4-1.2l-2-2.667A2 2 0 0 0 17 2H7a2 2 0 0 0-1.6.8z\"}],\"$undefined\"]}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col flex-1 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-white leading-snug\",\"children\":\"Power Banks\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-[#9999aa] leading-relaxed mt-1 flex-1\",\"children\":\"Survive longer Abyss runs on Amazon\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 flex items-center justify-between\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[11px] text-[#9999aa]\",\"children\":\"on Amazon\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[#D4A853] text-sm font-semibold group-hover:translate-x-0.5 transition-transform\",\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":\"Shop ↗\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"24:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}]]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"9d:I[27201,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/d2be314c3ece3fbe.js\"],\"IconMark\"]\n22:null\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"26:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Genshin Lunar Reactions Guide — Moonsign, Triggers, Scaling\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"How Genshin's Lunar and Stellar Glimmer reactions work: which characters enable them, Moonsign levels, CRIT rules and the 60/30/5/5 team damage split.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"author\",\"href\":\"https://gamertagmythras.com\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"author\",\"content\":\"Mythras\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"keywords\",\"content\":\"genshin lunar reactions,lunar-charged genshin,lunar-bloom explained,moonsign ascendant gleam,stellar-conduct genshin,stellar swirl reaction,can lunar reactions crit\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"creator\",\"content\":\"Mythras\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"name\":\"publisher\",\"content\":\"Mythras // The Multiverse\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"name\":\"googlebot\",\"content\":\"index, follow, max-video-preview:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"9\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://gamertagmythras.com/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"Genshin Lunar Reactions Guide — Moonsign, Triggers, Scaling\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"How Genshin's Lunar and Stellar Glimmer reactions work: which characters enable them, Moonsign levels, CRIT rules and the 60/30/5/5 team damage split.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"12\",{\"property\":\"og:url\",\"content\":\"https://gamertagmythras.com/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"13\",{\"property\":\"og:image\",\"content\":\"https://gamertagmythras.com/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/hero-columbina.webp\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"14\",{\"property\":\"og:image:alt\",\"content\":\"Columbina, the only character whose Moonsign Benediction passive converts Electro-Charged, Bloom and Hydro Crystallize into all three Lunar reactions at once.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"15\",{\"property\":\"og:type\",\"content\":\"article\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"16\",{\"property\":\"article:published_time\",\"content\":\"2026-08-17T00:00:00.000Z\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"17\",{\"property\":\"article:modified_time\",\"content\":\"2026-09-04T00:00:00.000Z\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"18\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"19\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"Genshin Lunar Reactions Guide — Moonsign, Triggers, Scaling\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"20\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"How Genshin's Lunar and Stellar Glimmer reactions work: which characters enable them, Moonsign levels, CRIT rules and the 60/30/5/5 team damage split.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"21\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image\",\"content\":\"https://gamertagmythras.com/images/blog/genshin-impact/genshin-lunar-reactions-guide/hero-columbina.webp\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"22\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.ico?favicon.0b3bf435.ico\",\"sizes\":\"256x256\",\"type\":\"image/x-icon\"}],[\"$\",\"$L9d\",\"23\",{}]]\n"])</script></body></html>